#**
The site's search results page, at /search: WeblogRequestMapper forwards
it to the search servlet for the site space, and the servlet renders this
template whatever theme the site space uses (a theme may ship its own
template named site-search; none of the bundled themes does), as PageServlet
does the discovery front page. A plain page: the site name as the one h1
linking home, the search form, the results, the site footer.

Data: $model is SearchResultsModel in its site view (one ranked list across
blogs, paged by ten); the results come from the showSearchResults macro,
untouched. $model.term is the query already escaped (escapeXml10), so it is
emitted bare; the site space's name comes escaped from the wrapper;
$config.siteName is raw and escaped here. The page is noindex (the
showSeoHead macro, since $model.searchResults is true) and never cached.

The form's markup (form.site-search, input[type=search][name=q]) is a
contract, and the showSiteSearchBox macro prints it for this page and for
the front page alike, so both post to the same address. The style
below has no hash and no dollar sign: Velocity would read either.
*#
<!DOCTYPE html>
## lang: WeblogWrapper#getLanguageTag, as page.vm explains.
<html lang="$model.weblog.getLanguageTag()">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="default-src 'none'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src * data:; frame-src https://www.youtube-nocookie.com https://player.vimeo.com; font-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; connect-src 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'">
    ## The themes' title rule, "Search: q — Site": both halves arrive escaped.
    #if($utils.isNotEmpty($model.term))
    <title>$utils.titleWithName($text.get("search.title", [$model.term]), $model.weblog.name)</title>
    #else
    <title>$utils.titleWithName($text.get("search.titleNone"), $model.weblog.name)</title>
    #end
    <link href="$url.absoluteSite/favicon.svg" rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" />
    ## The site space has no posts, so no feed autodiscovery.
    #showSeoHead()
    #showAnalyticsTrackingCode($model.weblog)
    <style>
body.site-search-page { color-scheme: light dark; margin: 0; background: Canvas; color: CanvasText;
    font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; line-height: 1.55; }
.site-search-page * { box-sizing: border-box; }
.site-search-wrap { max-width: 46rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 16px; }
.site-search-skip { position: absolute; left: -9999px; }
.site-search-skip:focus { left: 16px; top: 8px; padding: .25rem .5rem; background: Canvas; }
.site-search-mast { padding: 1.5rem 0 1rem; border-bottom: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 15%, transparent); }
.site-search-site { margin: 0; font-size: 1.5rem; line-height: 1.2; }
.site-search-site a { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
.site-search { display: flex; gap: .5rem; margin: 1.5rem 0 0; }
.site-search input[type=search] { flex: 1 1 auto; min-width: 0; padding: .5rem .625rem; font: inherit;
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 35%, transparent); border-radius: 6px; background: Canvas; color: inherit; }
.site-search button { padding: .5rem 1rem; font: inherit; border: 1px solid currentColor; border-radius: 6px;
    background: transparent; color: inherit; cursor: pointer; }
.site-search-empty, .site-search-error { margin: 1.5rem 0 0; }
.site-search-pager .search-summary { margin: 1rem 0 0; font-size: .875rem; }
.site-search-pager .search-pager { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin: 1rem 0 0; }
.site-search-foot { margin: 3rem 0 0; padding: 1.5rem 0 2rem; font-size: .875rem;
    border-top: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 15%, transparent); }
.site-search-foot ul { list-style: none; margin: 0 0 1rem; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .5rem 1.25rem; }
.site-search-foot a { color: inherit; }
    </style>
</head>
<body class="site-search-page">
<a class="site-search-skip" href="#main">$text.get("discovery.skip")</a>

<header class="site-search-mast">
    <div class="site-search-wrap">
        ## a list page: the site name is its h1 (docs/dev/themes-and-templates.md, the heading rule)
        <h1 class="site-search-site"><a href="$url.home">$utils.escapeHTML($config.siteName)</a></h1>
    </div>
</header>

<main id="main" class="site-search-wrap">
    ## The one search box (weblog.vm), filled with the query so far.
    #showSiteSearchBox($model.weblog $model.term)
    #set($pager = $model.getWeblogEntriesPager())
    #if($model.hits > 0 && ($model.siteScope || $model.blogOnly))
    ## A div, not a nav: the pager macro emits its own labelled nav.
    <div class="site-search-pager">
        #showNextPrevSearchControl($pager)
    </div>
    #end
    ## A failed search also reports zero hits, so the error comes first, in
    ## fixed words: the exception text is internal detail on a public page.
    #if($utils.isNotEmpty($model.errorMessage))
    <p class="site-search-error">$text.get("search.unavailable")</p>
    #elseif($utils.isNotEmpty($model.term) && $model.hits == 0 && $model.otherHits.isEmpty())
    <p class="site-search-empty">$text.get("search.siteEmpty")</p>
    #end
    #showSearchResults($model)
</main>

<footer class="site-search-foot">
    <div class="site-search-wrap">
        <nav aria-label="$text.get('discovery.siteNav')">
            <ul>
                <li><a href="$url.home">$text.get("discovery.frontPage")</a></li>
            #foreach($navPage in $model.getNavPages($model.weblog))
                <li><a href="$url.staticPage($navPage.slug)">$utils.escapeHTML($navPage.title)</a></li>
            #end
                <li><a href="$url.site/pressroom-ui/siteDirectory.rol">$text.get("discovery.directory")</a></li>
            </ul>
        </nav>
        #showColophon($model.weblog)
    </div>
</footer>
</body>
</html>
